s and metrics differ (values added, removed, or changed).\n- Comparison covers both training runs and Data Science Pipelines runs, reading run parameters and metrics through the interfaces the Dashboard already uses to surface runs.\n- No changes to run execution, storage, or the run pages' existing behavior (comparison is an additional view).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a list of runs, when the user selects two or more runs, then the Dashboard offers a comparison action that opens a side-by-side view of those runs' parameters and metrics.\n- Given a comparison of exactly two runs, then the view highlights which parameters and metrics differ between them.\n- Given a selection that includes Data Science Pipelines runs, then their parameters and metrics are presented in the comparison the same as training runs (passive validation of the Data Science Pipelines component — no code change there).\n- Given a run with missing parameters or metrics, then the comparison renders the missing values without breaking the view.\n- Existing run list and run detail pages continue to function unchanged.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics for two or more selected runs.\n- HLR-3 (P1, consolidated): diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs — a presentation mode of the same comparison surface, delivered in this epic.\n\n--- E002 ---\n\n# Link registered model versions to their producing runs\n\n## Description\n\nRecord, on each registered model version, a link back to the run that produced it, so downstream consumers (including the Dashboard) can resolve the producing run and open a comparison. Uses the Model Registry's existing model-version metadata extension point.\n\n## Scope\n\n- When a model version is registered from a run, store the identity of the producing run on the model version (e.g. via the registry's custom-properties extension point on ModelVersion entities).\n- E