{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3ee5a5d18bb64f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| Epic | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|------|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view in the Dashboard (side-by-side and diff) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Link registered model versions to their producing runs | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n20\t\n21\t## Dependency DAG\n22\t\n23\t```mermaid\n24\tgraph TD\n25\t    E001[\"E001 Run comparison view (Dashboard)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Open comparison from registry (Dashboard)\"]\n26\t    E002[\"E002 Registry run links (Model Registry)\"] --> E003\n27\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Documentation\"]\n28\t    E002 --> E004\n29\t    E003 --> E004\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\t## DAG Justification\n33\t\n34\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n35\t|------|------|-----------|\n36\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework/surface → consumer) | The registry entry point opens the run comparison capability; it builds on that surface and cannot ship before the comparison view exists. |\n37\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact → consuming Implementation) | The Dashboard registry entry point builds against the producing-run link the Model Registry stores and exposes on model versions. |\n38\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes the comparison workflow delivered from the runs list. |\n39\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation covers opening a comparison from the registry, which requires the run links. |\n40\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation covers the registry entry point. |\n41\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | The Dashboard comparison view and the Model Registry run-link metadata are independent changes in different components and repos; neither builds against the other's artifact. Both start immediately. |\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n44\t\n45\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n46\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n47\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics for two or more selected runs, covering both training and pipeline runs. |\n48\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E002, RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Split across components per the boundary rule: registry-side link storage (Model Registry) and Dashboard-side entry point. |\n49\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 (consolidated) | Redundant with HLR-1: the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data, for the same component and team. One capability, one epic, at the higher of the two priorities (P0). Splitting by priority label would produce two epics building the same surface plus an artificial serialization edge between them. |\n50\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Docs-authoring epic; per the docs-authoring priority exception its priority is derived from the strategy `priority: Major` field → P1. |\n51\t\n52\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n53\t\n54\t## Health Warnings\n55\t\n56\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), and no Non-Functional Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs; owner teams were inferred from the architecture context files (RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry, RHOAI Pipelines). Team assignments should be confirmed with the strategy author.\n57\t- **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines**: no DSP code change is implied; pipeline runs are already surfaced in the Dashboard and their parameters/metrics are readable through existing interfaces (data-science-pipelines.md). Validation that comparison works for pipeline runs is an acceptance criterion on the Dashboard comparison epic. If the RHOAI Pipelines team must independently validate pipeline-run comparison (the strategy's missing Impacted Teams table leaves this open), a separate validation epic owned by that team should be added.\n58\t- **Redundant HLRs consolidated**: the problem statement notes requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. HLR-1 and HLR-3 describe the same comparison surface and are covered by a single epic at P0 rather than split by priority label.\n59\t- **Docs priority above its HLR**: HLR-4 is P2, but the docs-authoring epic is P1 because the docs-authoring priority exception derives priority from the strategy's `priority: Major` field. This is per-rule; flagged for planner awareness.\n60\t- **Component mapping note**: all strategy components map verbatim to canonical names (Dashboard, Model Registry, Data Science Pipelines). The Documentation epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component; no non-obvious mappings were needed.\n61\t\n62\t## Tiered Delivery\n63\t\n64\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is in-platform.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee6e6abde0081a0","agent_id":"ab1af650465ed2dd3","session_id":"d7f44887-6b51-4892-b0d7-5d5cd7144188","uuid":"e28dad10-48a3-4ac7-a361-0e3526f510d8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:10:22.620Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3ee5a5d18bb64f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_ty