{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aad4e86c8eece511","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Link registered model versions to their producing runs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Link registered model versions to their producing runs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRecord, on each registered model version, a link back to the run that produced it, so that downstream consumers (including the Dashboard's registry UI) can resolve the producing run and open a comparison from the Model Registry. This establishes the training-lineage connection the registry's role calls for.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- When a model version is registered from a run, store the identity of the producing run on the model version, using the Model Registry's existing model-version metadata extension point (custom properties on ModelVersion entities).\n38\t- Expose the producing-run link through the registry's existing API surface so clients can resolve it.\n39\t- Backward compatibility: existing model versions without a producing-run link remain valid and are served unchanged.\n40\t- No changes to model serving, registration workflow semantics, or the registry's storage model beyond the added metadata.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a model version registered from a run, then the model version carries a resolvable link to the run that produced it.\n45\t- Given a client reading a model version through the registry's API, then the producing-run link is returned when present.\n46\t- Given an existing model version with no producing-run link, then it remains valid and is served unchanged.\n47\t- Given two model versions produced by different runs, then each carries its own correct link with no cross-contamination.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-2 (P1, registry side): registered model versions link back to the run that produced them.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee6e6abde0081a0","agent_id":"ab1af650465ed2dd3","session_id":"d7f44887-6b51-4892-b0d7-5d5cd7144188","uuid":"c719d854-2dc7-4944-8290-5c4c77a31d70","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:10:26.084Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aad4e86c8eece511","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
