uns; model-registry.md names training lineage and custom properties on ModelVersion as the extension point). E002's `pattern_precedent: 1` is corroborated by the same custom-properties documentation. E004's `human_process_gates: -1` is justified by the Red Hat docs content-process review gates; E003's `human_process_gates: 0` (cross-team coordination, no formal gate) is a reasonable borderline call. No type/signal-field mismatches.\n32\t\n33\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n34\tEvery epic has testable Given/When/Then-style ACs derived from the HLRs. Rule-mandated ACs are present: E004 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC, and there is no konflux chain or replacement work requiring rollback/feature-flag ACs (E002 is an additive extension and still carries backward-compatibility ACs). E001 includes an AC covering pipeline runs (passive DSP validation) and missing-value rendering; E003 includes graceful degradation for model versions without links. No externally-controlled preconditions are misfiled as ACs. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n35\t\n36\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n37\tAll strategy scope is covered: side-by-side comparison (E001), diff view (E001), registry run links (E002), registry entry point (E003), documentation from both entry points (E004). Out-of-scope constraints (no auto-promotion, no cross-cluster/project comparison) are respected and explicitly carried into E003's scope and E004's documented limitations. The Data Science Pipelines component is handled as passive with a validation AC on E001 and an explicit Health Warning offering a separate validation epic if the Pipelines team requires one. The strategy's missing sections (Impacted Teams, Dependencies, Given/When/Then ACs, NFRs) are flagged in Health Warnings rather than silently dropped; team assignments were inferred from architecture context and marked for confirmation.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83becb76b4647d78","agent_id":"a2c90e535fd